Susan: Yes, I did. I''d love to help out in a shelter. Think of all those cute little animals!
Jessie: Exactly. But maybe it''s too good to be true. What if we have to clean the smelly cages?
Susan: I''d hate that. Can we ask for gloves?
Jessie: Of course. How about you clean the outside of the cages, and I''ll clean the inside?
Susan: Thanks, Jessie, you''re a true friend. By the way, when do they need us?
Jessie: On Sunday mornings, not Saturdays. So let''s not just talk about it — let''s do it!', 'Jessie 提到动物收容所的广告,觉得适合做志愿项目;Susan 愿意去帮忙,喜欢小动物;两人担心要清理脏笼子,决定要手套、并分工(一人擦外、一人擦里);时间是周日上午;两人决定行动起来。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What volunteer project are the girls talking about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Helping out at an animal shelter.","Teaching at a village school.","Building a new house.","Selling cute toys."]},{"q":"What are they worried about having to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Pay a lot of money.","Clean the smelly cages.","Walk a long way.","Cook for the animals."]},{"q":"What does Jessie suggest asking for?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Gloves.","More money.","A day off.","A bigger room."]},{"q":"How do they decide to divide the work?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Susan does everything alone.","One cleans outside, the other inside.","They will not clean at all.","Jessie does it all herself."]},{"q":"When does the shelter need them?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["On Saturday afternoons.","Every evening.","On Sunday mornings.","Only on holidays."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4');
But those who do it often say that they gain just as much in return.
Helping people who have less teaches us to be grateful for what we have.
It also gives our own lives a deeper sense of purpose.
In the end, when we share with others, we help ourselves to grow as well.', '许多年轻人以为志愿服务只是付出;但参与者常说自己得到的同样多;帮助拥有更少的人,教会我们对所拥有的心怀感恩;它也让我们的生活更有目标感;最终,当我们与人分享时,我们自己也在成长。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many young people think volunteering is about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Making a lot of money.","Becoming famous.","Travelling for fun.","Only giving to others."]},{"q":"What do volunteers often say they gain?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Just as much in return.","Nothing at all.","Only tiredness.","A higher salary."]},{"q":"What does helping those with less teach us?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To waste more.","To be grateful for what we have.","To stop sharing.","To ignore others."]},{"q":"What else does volunteering give our lives?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["More free money.","A longer holiday.","A deeper sense of purpose.","An easier job."]},{"q":"What happens when we share with others?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["We always lose something.","We become unhappy.","We have less to do.","We help ourselves to grow too."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4');
Mei: I think books would be best. Many of them have nothing to read at home.
Liu: That''s a good idea. But some people want to give money instead.
Mei: Money is useful too, but it is hard to be sure how it is spent.
Liu: True. Maybe we could give both books and some warm clothes.
Mei: Perfect. And we could spend a day there, reading with the children.
Liu: Yes! Giving our time may matter even more than giving things.', '刘和梅讨论给乡村贫困儿童捐什么;梅认为捐书最好,因为很多孩子家里没书读;有人想捐钱,但梅说钱难以确定用途;两人决定既捐书也捐保暖衣物;还打算去那里陪孩子读书;刘说付出时间也许比捐物更重要。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Mei think is the best thing to donate?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Books.","Money.","Toys.","Food."]},{"q":"Why is Mei unsure about giving money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is too heavy.","It is hard to be sure how it is spent.","Children do not like it.","It is against the rules."]},{"q":"What do they finally decide to give?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only money.","Nothing at all.","Both books and warm clothes.","Just one old book."]},{"q":"What else do they plan to do at the village?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sell some toys.","Build a new school.","Take photos only.","Read with the children."]},{"q":"What does Liu say may matter even more than giving things?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Giving their time.","Giving more money.","Giving advice.","Giving nothing."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4');
Some young people have decided to do something about this waste.
They collect food that shops can no longer sell and hand it out to families in need.
In this simple way, food that would be wasted is shared with hungry people.
Sharing what we have, they say, is much better than throwing it away.', '城市里每天都有大量好食物被扔掉;一些年轻人决定为此做点事;他们收集商店卖不出去的食物,分发给有需要的家庭;通过这种简单的方式,本会被浪费的食物被分享给饥饿的人;他们说,分享所有比扔掉好得多。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does the passage describe?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Too few shops in the city.","Good food being thrown away.","Children with no school.","Rivers full of rubbish."]},{"q":"Who decided to act on this problem?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The city''s shop owners.","A group of doctors.","Some young people.","Foreign visitors."]},{"q":"What do they do with the food they collect?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They sell it again.","They keep it for themselves.","They throw it into the sea.","They hand it out to families in need."]},{"q":"What happens to food that would be wasted?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is shared with hungry people.","It is burned.","It is hidden away.","It is left to rot."]},{"q":"What do these young people believe?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Wasting food saves time.","Sharing is better than throwing food away.","Shops should sell more food.","Food should never be given away."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4');
Tom: It''s hard, Mum. There''s no electricity here, and the children have only pencils and paper.
Mum: That sounds tough. Are you managing all right?
Tom: I am, slowly. I''ve had to be more imaginative and less rigid about the rules.
Mum: I''m proud of you. Do you feel you are making a difference?
Tom: At first I wasn''t sure. But the children love to learn, and that keeps me going.
Mum: Then it''s worth it. By the way, your parcel of sweets is on its way!', '妈妈打电话问 Tom 海外支教的情况;Tom 说很辛苦,没有电,孩子们只有铅笔和纸;他在慢慢适应,变得更有创意、不那么死板;妈妈为他自豪,问他是否觉得有意义;Tom 起初不确定,但孩子们爱学习让他坚持下去;妈妈说那就值得,并告诉他寄的糖果包裹在路上了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where is Tom and what is he doing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Studying at a city university.","Working in a shop.","Teaching as a volunteer far from home.","Travelling on holiday."]},{"q":"What is one difficulty Tom mentions?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["There are too many teachers.","The children have too many books.","The school is too modern.","There is no electricity."]},{"q":"How has Tom had to change his teaching?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By being more imaginative and less rigid.","By using more machines.","By being stricter with rules.","By giving up quickly."]},{"q":"What keeps Tom going?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The high pay.","The children''s love of learning.","The easy work.","The modern classrooms."]},{"q":"What does his mum say is on its way?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A new teacher.","A laptop.","A parcel of sweets.","A car."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4');
You came a long way to spend time with us and to lend a hand.
The books and warm clothes you brought will help us through the winter.
But more than the gifts, we are grateful for your kindness and your smiles.
We hope that one day we, too, can pay it forward and help someone else.', '代表这里所有的孩子,我要感谢来访的客人;你们远道而来陪伴我们、伸出援手;你们带来的书和暖衣将帮我们度过冬天;但比起礼物,我们更感激你们的善意和笑容;我们希望有一天自己也能把善意传递下去,去帮助别人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is the speaker thanking?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The local shopkeepers.","The school teachers only.","The children''s parents.","The visitors who came to help."]},{"q":"What did the visitors come to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To spend time and lend a hand.","To sell some books.","To take photos for a paper.","To open a new shop."]},{"q":"What will the books and clothes help with?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Making the school bigger.","Getting through the winter.","Selling at the market.","Painting the classroom."]},{"q":"What are the children most grateful for?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The amount of money.","The size of the gifts.","The visitors'' kindness and smiles.","The new building."]},{"q":"What do the children hope to do one day?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Forget the visitors.","Keep everything for themselves.","Stop going to school.","Pay it forward and help someone else."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4');

